# AGENTS.md

nbkp is an rsync-based backup tool for sources and destinations that come and go.

## Commands

- `mise run preflight-quick`: every lint and the fast tests, before each commit.
- `mise run preflight`: every lint and test CI runs, every few commits and before review.
- `mise run fmt` after editing any file.
- `mise tasks` lists the rest.
- An agent has no mise-activated shell, so run a mise task when one does the job,
  `uv run --no-sync <tool>` for a tool in the project's environment, and `mise exec -- <tool>` for
  one mise installs ([why](https://github.com/iglootools/common/blob/main/guidelines/project-setup/python-tooling.md#invoke-tools-through-uv-run---no-sync-tool-in-mise-tasks-not-bare)).

## Guidelines

The shared iglootools guidelines govern every change. Claude Code loads their indexes through
the `iglootools` plugin. Other agents: read [iglootools/common's
index](https://github.com/iglootools/common/blob/main/guidelines/README.md) and the `README.md`
of each directory it lists, then, before any change, every guideline their rows send you to. Read
[docs/guidelines.md](docs/guidelines.md) before any change too: it holds this project's deviations
and its own rules, and links to the project's other guidelines files.

## Where things are

[CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) indexes every document, from setup to the domain and the
architecture. Read a document when the task reaches it, not up front.
